STATUTORY DURABLE FINANCIAL POWER OF ATTORNEY
General & Financial Asset Management Mandate
NOTICE: THE POWERS GRANTED BY THIS DOCUMENT ARE BROAD AND SWEEPING. IF 
YOU HAVE ANY QUESTIONS ABOUT THESE POWERS, OBTAIN COMPETENT LEGAL 
ADVICE. THIS DOCUMENT DOES NOT AUTHORIZE ANYONE TO MAKE MEDICAL AND 
OTHER HEALTH-CARE DECISIONS FOR YOU. YOU MAY REVOKE THIS POWER OF 
ATTORNEY IF YOU LATER WISH TO DO SO.
Article I: APPOINTMENT OF AGENT (ATTORNEY-IN-FACT)
Section 1.01 Principal & Primary Agent: I, ARTHUR PENDELTON, residing at 742 Evergreen 
Terrace, Austin, TX 78701, hereby appoint Eleanor Vance Pendelton, residing at 742 Evergreen 
Terrace, Austin, TX 78701, Phone: (512) 555-0143, as my Agent (attorney-in-fact) to act for me 
in any lawful way with respect to the subjects initialed in Article II below.
Section 1.02 Successor Agent(s): If Eleanor Vance Pendelton resigns, dies, becomes 
incapacitated, is not qualified to serve, or declines to serve, I appoint Graham M. Pendelton, 
residing at 1040 West Peachtree St, Atlanta, GA 30309, Phone: (404) 555-0199, as my 
successor Agent. If he is also unable or unwilling to serve, I appoint Clara Vance, residing at 
1802 South Congress Ave, Austin, TX 78704, Phone: (512) 555-0188, as second alternate 
Agent.
Article II: GRANT OF GENERAL POWERS
TO GRANT ALL OF THE FOLLOWING POWERS, INITIAL THE LINE IN FRONT OF (O) AND 
IGNORE THE LINES IN FRONT OF THE OTHER POWERS:
____ (A) Real property transactions;
____ (B) Tangible personal property transactions;
____ (C) Stock and bond transactions;
____ (D) Commodity and option transactions;
____ (E) Banking and other financial institution transactions;
____ (F) Business operating transactions;
____ (G) Insurance and annuity transactions;
____ (H) Estate, trust, and other beneficiary transactions;
____ (I) Claims and litigation;
____ (J) Personal and family maintenance;
____ (K) Benefits from social security, Medicare, Medicaid, or other governmental programs;
____ (L) Retirement plan transactions;
